# Cloudflare Pages response headers. `output: "export"` copies public/ into out/
# verbatim, so this ships with the build; it is inert anywhere else.
#
# ── Caching ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is the whole of "clear your cache to be able to log in". Every HTML
# document names content-hashed chunks under /_next/static/, and a deploy
# replaces every one of those names. A browser still holding yesterday's HTML
# asks the new deployment for chunk files it does not have, gets the 404 page
# back where a script should be, and React never hydrates: the Google button is
# inert, and /auth/callback never stores the token Google just handed it. The
# page cannot fix itself, because nothing on the page is running — clearing the
# cache by hand was the only way out.
#
# So: an HTML document may never be reused without asking us first, and the
# hashed assets may be kept forever (a new build gives them new names, so there
# is nothing to invalidate — that is what the hash is for).
#
# The specific rule comes last on purpose. Cloudflare applies every matching rule
# and the later value wins for a repeated header, so /_next/static keeps
# `immutable` instead of inheriting must-revalidate from /*. If that ever stops
# being true the assets are merely revalidated more often than they need to be —
# a 304, not a broken page. The ordering is an optimisation; the /* rule is the
# fix.
#
# ── Security ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The session JWT lives in localStorage (lib/api.ts) as a bearer credential
# nothing can revoke, so script injection == account takeover. There is no server
# to set headers, and no nonce is possible in a static export — this file is the
# only place a CSP can come from.
#
# connect-src pins the API. If the API ever moves off b3-api.duckdns.org, this
# line moves with it or every request in the app fails.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://b3-api.duckdns.org; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
